    <statement><p>Each page of a book consists of a header, a footer and the middle part. The header is <m>{{\frac{7}{9}}}</m> inches in height; the footer is <m>{{\frac{17}{18}}}</m> inches in height; and the middle part is <m>{6{\textstyle\frac{4}{9}}}</m> inches in height.</p>
<p>What is the total height of each page in this book? Use mixed number in your answer if needed.</p>
<p>Each page in this book is <fillin characters="11" name="AnSwEr0001"/> inches in height.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>8{\textstyle\frac{1}{6}}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p>We add up the height of the header, middle part and footer to find the total height of a page:</p>
<p><m>\displaystyle{ 
\begin{aligned}[t]
   {{\frac{7}{9}}} + {6{\textstyle\frac{4}{9}}} + {{\frac{17}{18}}}
      \amp =    {{\frac{7}{9}}} + 6 + {{\frac{4}{9}}} + {{\frac{17}{18}}} \\
      \amp =    6 + {{\frac{7}{9}}} + {{\frac{4}{9}}} + {{\frac{17}{18}}} \\
      \amp = 6 + \frac{7\cdot2}{9\cdot2} + \frac{4\cdot2}{9\cdot2} + \frac{17}{18}  \\
      \amp = 6 + \frac{14}{18} +  \frac{8}{18} + \frac{17}{18} \\
      \amp = 6 + \frac{14+8+17}{18} \\
      \amp = 6 + \frac{39}{18} \\
      \amp = 6 + \frac{13}{6} \\
      \amp = 6 + 2 \frac{1}{6} \\
      \amp = {8{\textstyle\frac{1}{6}}}
\end{aligned}
    }</m></p>
<p>Each page in this book is <m>{8{\textstyle\frac{1}{6}}}</m> inches in height.</p>
</solution>
